The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of the variable `i` in the `FindLength` function, where it was declared outside of the loop, leading to potential logical errors in the loop's iteration count. This made the check on `i` ineffective, as it was not being incremented properly within the loop, which could result in an infinite loop or incorrect behavior when processing the demuxing logic.

